4.  **`CC(=O)C=CC1=CC=C(C=C1)O`** and **`CC(=O)/C=C/C1=CC=C(C=C1)O`**: These p-coumaric acid derivatives provide consistent binding to the key residues PHE360, PHE440, and TYR366, with scores of -7.4 and -7.3 respectively. They maintain good Lipinski properties and are readily available.

All suggested molecules are structurally distinct from the initial list and were screened to ensure they are not simple chain-length extensions of fatty acids. Each binds to at least two of the specified critical residues, ensuring high specificity for the MCR enzyme binding site.
